# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template, which holds variable NAMES only and is committed so a
# fresh clone knows what to set. The `.env*` glob above would swallow it.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Scratch directories that are NOT part of the website.
#
# `git add -A` swept both of these into a commit once, along with eight font
# binaries and a pile of Python bytecode, so they are ignored explicitly rather
# than left to happen again. Neither is built, served or imported by the site.
#
#   lokesh-rohilla-logo/  logo design scratch: concepts, renders, font files and
#                         the scripts that generated them
#   logo-design-skill/    a separate git repository in its own right; committing
#                         it added a gitlink, which clones as an empty broken
#                         submodule reference rather than as the files
#
# IGNORE THESE OR MOVE THEM OUTSIDE THE REPO. If the logo work should be kept,
# it belongs in its own repository, not alongside the site it designs for.
lokesh-rohilla-logo/
logo-design-skill/
__pycache__/
